        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall where the root श्वठ falls in the Dhatupatha, checking whether it belongs to the Curadi class and what meaning is traditionally assigned to it.\n\nFound it: श्वठ belongs to the kathādi (adanta) group listed as \"शठ श्वठ सम्यगवभाषणे.\" Since it's adanta, the final अ is dropped before णिच् by अतो लोपः, and since this lopa is sthānivat, there's no upadhā vṛddhi — giving श्वठयति, with the Lit form श्वठयाञ्चकार / श्वठयाम्बभूव / श्वठयामास.\n\n",
